ui2/frontend/src/auth/adminApi.ts reads the token like this, and its own file header already calls the gap a disclosed, temporary limitation:

async function csrfToken(): Promise<string | undefined> {
  try {
    const response = await fetch("/session/status", { credentials: "include" });
    const body = await response.json();
    return typeof body?.csrf_token === "string" ? body.csrf_token : undefined;
  } catch {
    return undefined;
  }
}

ui2/service/.../api/SessionStatusController.java builds its body with exactly these keys and no other -- the string `csrf` does not appear anywhere in that file:

        body.put("authenticated", true);
        Optional<LocalCredentialRecord> identity = localIdentityResolver.resolve(session.get().actorFingerprint());
        identity.ifPresent(record -> {
            body.put("display_name", record.localIdentityName());
            body.put("must_change_password", enforcePasswordChangeOnFirstLogin && record.mustChangePassword());
            List<String> roleTokens = ...;
            body.put("role_tokens", roleTokens);
